7️⃣ Flashcards 🃏
Q: Which 5 aggregate functions? → COUNT, SUM, AVG, MIN, MAX
Q: COUNT(*) vs COUNT(col)? → * counts all rows; col skips NULLs
Q: What does GROUP BY do? → Splits rows into buckets; aggregate runs per bucket
Q: Golden rule of SELECT + GROUP BY? → Every non-aggregated column must be in GROUP BY
Q: WHERE vs HAVING? → WHERE filters rows (before grouping); HAVING filters groups (after)
Q: Can WHERE use SUM()? → No — aggregates don't exist until after WHERE runs
Q: Can HAVING use role = 'Engineer' (no aggregate)? → Yes but shouldn't — use WHERE
Q: Fastest way to get total years of Engineers only? → WHERE role = 'Engineer' then SUM()
Q: Execution order again? → FROM → WHERE → GROUP BY → HAVING → SELECT → ORDER BY → TOP
Q: Does AVG count NULLs in its average? → No — NULLs are skipped entirely


